      "error": "",
      "summary": "The probe runner change broadens kind-'test' execution from a single target file to full unittest discovery under its directory, which can produce incorrect verdicts for the requested target. I also found a new false-positive wiring error path in shadow probe invocation caused by catching all TypeError exceptions from the probe implementation.",
      "findings": [
        {
          "id": "b9e2819976fe",
          "rule": "",
          "severity": "major",
          "category": "correctness",
          "file": "src/codereview/probe.py",
          "line": 194,
          "title": "kind-'test' now runs every matching test in the directory, not just the requested target",
          "evidence": "The new unittest invocation discovers tests from the target directory using the target basename as a pattern, so a request for one file can execute additional matching files and fail or pass based on unrelated tests in that directory.",
          "evidence_quote": "                    \"discover\", \"-s\", start,",
          "recommendation": "Limit execution to the requested test module or file instead of directory-wide discovery. For unittest, derive the module path for the exact target and invoke it directly, or otherwise constrain discovery so unrelated files cannot affect the verdict.",
